WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.210
Let's make a call feel like an actual conversation, not a sequence of announcements.

2
00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:06.000
That means being able to interrupt it, and tuning how it delivers speech.

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:06.749
Turn on barge-in.

4
00:00:06.749 --> 00:00:12.872
Now you can talk over the avatar to interrupt it — the moment you start speaking, it stops and listens, exactly like interrupting a person.

5
00:00:12.872 --> 00:00:16.000
No waiting for it to finish a paragraph you've already heard enough of.

6
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.692
Here's the important gotcha, and you should demonstrate it.

7
00:00:18.692 --> 00:00:24.304
Barge-in through speakers makes the app hear its own voice and interrupt itself, over and over — it's unusable on speakers.

8
00:00:24.304 --> 00:00:25.627
Headphones fix it completely.

9
00:00:25.627 --> 00:00:28.000
If barge-in seems broken, this is almost always why.

10
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.122
In Settings, Voice, a few controls change how it sounds.

11
00:00:30.122 --> 00:00:31.449
Human delivery adds natural pacing.

12
00:00:31.449 --> 00:00:33.420
Expressiveness goes zero, one, two — flat to lively.

13
00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:34.405
Persona shapes its manner.

14
00:00:34.405 --> 00:00:41.000
And Speech rewrite is clever: a small model rewrites each reply for the ear — numbers become words, markdown is stripped, sentences get shorter — so it reads aloud naturally.

15
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.101
One common complaint: it hears me but doesn't reply.

16
00:00:43.101 --> 00:00:43.990
Two controls fix that.

17
00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:46.657
The level meter shows whether it's actually picking up your voice.

18
00:00:46.657 --> 00:00:53.000
And silence timeout, plus smart endpointing, decide how long a pause means you're done — turn them up if it keeps cutting you off, down if it waits too long.

19
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:53.910
It now converses naturally.

20
00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:59.000
Last in the voice module, we replace the plain orb with an actual 3D character — and cover the licensing question before you put one on a public video.

